I think that one of the prime skills for Nethack is to rapidly be able to
ascertain what is and isn't ordinary about a given situation --
especially in an environment with lots of bones files.  I seem to have a
talent for noticing things that don't "match", and it helps in NH.

FREX: A kobold in a room is ordinary.  A kobold in a room with a hobbit
corpse, on the other hand, is the signal that you may be on a bones
level (could be a rock trap, though) and should proceed with caution.

> What about the wand of cold or the horn of fire that the
> first kobold you meet has already picked up?

Those are no different than that same kobold (or gnome, or whatever)
happening to spawn with one.  It's fairly rare, and also fairly rare
that you're in such bad shape that either will be an instakill; you
have to spot it on the first zap (which may even miss!) and then decide 
_from there_ how you'll get out of the situation.  Each situation will
be different; usually there is an escape, even if that escape is simply
"running away" -- critters won't zap past a certain range.

It's like the Gnome with the Wand of Death.  It's an amusing meme, and
does even occasionally happen, but it just won't happen anywhere often
enough that you should bother worrying about it -- other than getting
reflection or MR at the first opportunity, which you were going to do 
anyway.

